---
import type { Category, LocaleCode } from '../../i18n/types';
import { getLocaleConfig } from '../../data/locales';

export interface Props {
  locale: LocaleCode;
  category: Category;
}
const { locale } = Astro.props;
const config = getLocaleConfig(locale);
---

<section class="mx-auto mt-10 max-w-4xl px-4 pb-12" aria-labelledby="calculator-resource-heading">
  <div class="grid gap-8 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm sm:p-8">
    <div>
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[.14em] text-accent">
        Transparent estimate
      </p>
      <h2 id="calculator-resource-heading" class="mt-2 text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">
        How this calculator works
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-600">
        Enter the supported information above to get an estimate for your selected country or region. The
        result is calculated using the rules built into this specific calculator, then displayed
        in {config.currency} using the local number format.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-600">
        A simple way to check the result is to compare the gross amount you entered with the
        deductions and final amount shown in the breakdown. The exact result depends on the pay
        frequency, tax year, location, filing choices, and other inputs supported by the page.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900">What is generally included?</h3>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 leading-7 text-slate-600">
          <li>The inputs and pay frequency you selected.</li>
          <li>Country- or state-specific rates and thresholds supported by the calculator.</li>
          <li>A formatted result and, where available, a breakdown of major deductions.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900">What may be excluded?</h3>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 leading-7 text-slate-600">
          <li>
            Employer benefits, credits, dependents, or deductions that were not part of the
            calculator inputs.
          </li>
          <li>Local, municipal, or regional rules that are not listed on the page.</li>
          <li>
            Collective agreements, unusual legal exceptions, and employer-specific payroll
            rounding.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-5">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900">Data year, sources, and assumptions</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 leading-7 text-slate-600">
        Where a calculator uses a specific tax year, the page identifies it. The current release
        focuses on 2026 data where a tax year is shown. Before relying on an estimate for an
        important decision, review the relevant source notes on the{' '}
        <a class="font-semibold text-accent underline" href="/data-sources/">
          Data Sources
        </a>{' '}
        page and the{' '}
        <a class="font-semibold text-accent underline" href="/how-calculators-work/">
          methodology
        </a>{' '}
        page.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900">Frequently asked questions</h3>
      <div class="mt-3 divide-y divide-slate-200 rounded-xl border border-slate-200">
        <details class="p-4">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-slate-800">
            Why is my result different from my payslip?
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-2 leading-7 text-slate-600">
            Your actual payslip may include employer-specific withholding, benefits, credits, local
            taxes, deductions, or rounding that the calculator does not model.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details class="p-4">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-slate-800">
            Can I use this as official tax advice?
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-2 leading-7 text-slate-600">
            No. PayRenTax provides general informational estimates. For a filing, employment,
            legal, or financial decision, confirm the details with the appropriate authority or a
            qualified professional.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details class="p-4">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-slate-800">
            What if my country or region is not supported?
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-2 leading-7 text-slate-600">
            Do not use another country or state as a substitute. Choose a calculator that matches
            your jurisdiction and check the page for any unsupported-input warnings.
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
